  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Freeze and free – with a ball",
  "description": "Everyone has a stick and a ball and skates freely inside a square of cones. A hunter (red) also has a ball and tries to hit the others’ balls by passing at them. If your ball is hit you freeze: stand still with your blade on the ball. A team-mate frees you by skating a lap round you with their ball. Whoever frees the most wins.\n\nThe hunter passes along the ice – no lofted balls and no hard hits at team-mates. For the youngest: start without balls and let the hunter freeze someone with a touch of the hand. Change hunter often, and use two hunters in a big group. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – where is the hunter and where is the free ice?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to the stick so you can turn quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Use crossovers as you skate round a frozen team-mate."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Hunter: pass along the ice and aim at the ball, never at the skates."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
